// The contract between the host and every instrument.
//
// The host runs one copy of the instrument per finger (MPE channel) and sets
// these five controls on it. What each control DOES is up to the instrument.
//
//   freq      Hz. Pitch bend is already applied, so glides just work.
//   gate      1 while the finger is down, 0 after it lifts.
//   pressure  0..1, how hard this finger presses (channel aftertouch).
//   slide     0..1, finger position up/down the key (CC74).
//   velocity  0..1, how hard the note was struck. Fixed for the whole note.
//   legato    1 if the note started while another note of this instrument was sounding (or
//             had just ended): a slur. Fixed for the whole note. Optional; most ignore it.
//
// A note starts with gate going 0 -> 1 on a freshly cleared instrument, so
// `gate > gate'` is a reliable "note started" trigger.
//
// Optional: an instrument may also define `post`, one input and one or two outputs. The host
// then adds up all the voices and runs one copy of `post` on the sum (an instrument body,
// a reverb: anything linear that every note shares), instead of each voice doing it.

freq     = hslider("freq", 440, 20, 5000, 0.01);
gate     = hslider("gate", 0, 0, 1, 1);
pressure = hslider("pressure", 0, 0, 1, 0.001);
slide    = hslider("slide", 0.5, 0, 1, 0.001);
velocity = hslider("velocity", 0.5, 0, 1, 0.001);
legato   = hslider("legato", 0, 0, 1, 1);

// 1 for exactly one sample when a note starts.
trigger = gate > gate';
